description.notes:
- DO NOT remove any columns or relationships that are actively used in the system, but feel free to comment on their lines for improvement;
- DO NOT change the type of any already defined column, but feel free to suggest new types through comments on their lines;
- Delete all redundant constants in the Models, such as representing the array of fillables before the own $fillable itself;
- If suitable, add $casts, $with, $appends;
- Always include DC::TABLE_CREATOR and 'id' as $guarded, NEVER as $fillable;
- Always leverage the existing traits for audit columns;
- All new columns should be made ->nullable(), but if you should NEVER be nullable in a production system, leave a comment at the line pointing to that observation, mentioning they are nullable just for initial tests;
- For fields that follow specific and rigid law patterns, follow the laws of Brazil;
- Make sure that ::booted method calls parent::booted() and imposes the constraints at Model level;
- It is not necessary to add comments explaining each column, unless it is something non-trivial, needing rethinking or described in previous points;
- For one line statements and if possible, always suppress the brackets;
